Subject: parboot: providing inits and avoiding SE ?
Message-ID: <SQRm8eX6NjM.Hyh8neD9qIIJ@unmarked.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/unmarked/c/SQRm8eX6NjM/m/Hyh8neD9qIIJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Dear unmarked ones,

I have a rather complex dynamic occupancy model (i.e., with covariates on all params) for which I would like to get a bootstrap GOF assessment using the code in the colext vignette. Getting MLEs takes about 1100 secs, but providing inits and avoiding to compute SEs drastically reduces run time.

Is it possible to specify in parboot inits and the choice SE=FALSE ?

Thanks and kind regards  --  Marc

From u527e14923215b7e4 at groups.google.com  Thu Nov  3 15:20:27 2011
From: u527e14923215b7e4 at groups.google.com (Richard Chandler)
Date: Thu, 03 Nov 2011 15:20:27 +0000
Subject: Re: [unmarked] parboot: providing inits and avoiding SE ?
Message-ID: <SQRm8eX6NjM.EVDZg21hDrQJ@unmarked.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <SQRm8eX6NjM.Hyh8neD9qIIJ@unmarked.groups.google.com>
References: <SQRm8eX6NjM.Hyh8neD9qIIJ@unmarked.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/unmarked/c/SQRm8eX6NjM/m/EVDZg21hDrQJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi Marc,

parboot automatically sets se=FALSE, and uses the MLEs as the starting values. The code can be seen using the confusing command:

       getMethod("parboot", "unmarkedFit")

Note the key line:

        fits[[i]] <- update(object, data = simdata, starts = ests, se = FALSE)

Let me know if you see room for improvement.

Richard

